But actually — does NativeTabs render its own header? No, NativeTabs doesn't show headers by default. Good.

Let me think about whether to keep the `explore` tab. User chose "Home + Seasons (Recommended)" which said "Tabs become Home, Seasons, (keep Explore or drop it)". Hmm the option text said "(keep Explore or drop it)". The user selected that. So we can drop Explore. Let me drop explore tab since the recommended description implies Home + Seasons. Actually the option said "Tabs become Home, Seasons, (keep Explore or drop it)". Ambiguous. I'll drop Explore to keep it simple — it's template cruft. Actually, let me keep the plan minimal: remove explore.tsx and its tab. The user said "Home + Seasons (Recommended)" for tab layout which I described as "Replace Explore with Seasons, keeping two tabs" in the third option... wait no.

